/ Fix, then go on from the same step: Work reads a file that isn't there yet, and its handler fixes the cause (writes
/ the file), then starts the error's callback. The callback goes on from the read, in an app of its own: the read runs
/ again, finds the file, and the run goes on to its end, answering what it read. The handler checks that answer; the
/ resumed run never reaches the handler, as its read no longer fails.
Start
- call Work

/ The step that fails while the file is missing, its handler the fix.
Work
- read file 'workspace/needed.txt', write to %content%, on error call CaptureCallback
- return %content%

/ The fix, then the run goes on from the step that failed.
CaptureCallback
- write "fixed" to file 'workspace/needed.txt'
- set %cb% = %!error.callback%
- callback.start callback=%cb%, write to %resumed%
- assert %resumed% equals "fixed", "the callback's run should go on from the read"
- delete file 'workspace/needed.txt'
